### 8. Recommended Title Options (ranked)

1. **"You're Bad at Delegation — That's Why Your AI Agents Keep Failing"** — specific, provocative, makes the real problem impossible to dismiss. A CTO reads this and either agrees (already knows they have a delegation problem) or disagrees (immediately wants to argue). Both responses drive a click. Strongest for shareability and engagement.

2. **"Agentic AI Is Not a Technology Problem. It's a People Problem."** — clear thesis, credible, executive-facing. Less provocative than option 1 but broader in appeal. Better for an audience that is still defining its relationship with AI adoption.

3. **"The One Skill That Determines Whether Your AI Agents Actually Work"** — curiosity-gap structure, slightly softer. Trades some specificity for accessibility. Good for audiences earlier in their AI adoption thinking.

